From e4e67d0576b9c323170f71eac2adf8b50322f5a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:18:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cron): carry conservative integer context across shell
 walks [daveey]

An integer declaration was recognized only in the current text, so eval dequoting lost the arithmetic context. Expanded declare names/options and sourced declarations were not visible to the lexical hint. Keep a per-scan sticky hint, recognize opaque declaration boundaries without executing text, and include the hint in quote and path-visit scopes. Read extra subscript references conservatively; harmless twins and non-integer controls stay allowed.

Proof: isolated Bash markers reproduced two eval misses on base and six expansion/source misses before the second fix; focused GREEN 16 tests. Full lifecycle consumers and scripts/check follow before canonical publication.
